<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6744" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carbōnārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		1. carbo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>relating to
			charcoal</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">negotium,</span>”
				<i>traffic in charcoal</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aur.
						Vict. Vir. Ill. 72</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carbōnārĭus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>a burner of
				charcoal</i>, <i>a collier</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas.
				2, 8, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			4302</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carbōnārĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> (Sc. fornax.) <i>A furnace for charcoal</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Tert. Car. Christ.
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			(Sc. femina.) <i>The Charcoal-Woman</i>, <i>the title of a lost play by Plautus</i>, <i><span class="en">Fest.
				p. 30, 27</span></i> Müll.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
